  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-08-13T08:46:38.044Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Version:\nSteam release 2020-08-12\nDescription of the bug:\nWhen you're in fullbody tracking and you lower your head below the value of 0.68 you'll see the toes on the left foot point upwards as in the crouching animation. Unbinding the toes in the humanoid rig \"fixes the issue\". I'm not able to reproduce this on avatar2.0 avatars.\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\n1. Start VRChat and load into an avatar 3.0 with a humanoid rig configured with toes.\n2. Calibrate your fullbody tracking\n3. Lay down on a couch or a bed(Height of your viewpoint should be within crouching range)\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots):",
